    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d159">

                <pb facs="0258" n="156" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg156"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/1956: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Macy</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-07-29T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 29, 1927—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>23. Department’s mail instruction 334, March 4.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Please hand following note to Liberian Secretary of State: <quote
                            rend="blockquote">
                            <p>“With reference to the Legations’s note of April 19, 1927,<anchor
                                    n="33" xml:id="d159-f1"/> I have the honor to state that I have
                                been instructed to inform Your Excellency that the President and the
                                Secretary of State of the United States, having been advised that
                                suitable provision has been made for the extinguishment of the 1912
                                Loan, take pleasure in assuming the functions assigned to them under
                                the terms of the Loan Agreement of September 1, 1926.</p>
                            <p>“I am further instructed to inform Your Excellency that in pursuance
                                of Article 8 of that Agreement the President of the United States
                                hereby designates to the President of Liberia the name of Sidney de
                                la Rue for appointment as Financial Adviser to the Republic of
                                Liberia.”</p>
                        </quote></item>
                    <pb facs="0259" n="157" xml:id="pg157"/>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>After de la Rue has received his formal appointment you may call his
                        attention to the requirement of Article 9 that he report to the Department
                        the names of nominees for the positions therein provided.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>The Department understands that Major Staten and Captain Outley have
                        contracts with the Liberian Government and therefore it will take no action
                        under Article 12, paragraph 3, during the life of those contracts.</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
